# What must never reach a built image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is built in.
# Configuration - `.env` above all, which holds the signing keys and database
# credentials - is injected at run time and never built in: a file deleted in a
# later layer is still readable in the earlier one.
#
# Plugins are installable: the Dockerfile copies the plugin trees explicitly, so
# putting a directory there and rebuilding works as the install documentation
# describes. Only their `.env` files and tests are excluded.

# ---- secrets and local configuration ----
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ---- version control and editor state ----
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# ---- runtime data mounts, not code ----
/original
/webfiles
/userfiles
/temporal
/uploads

# ---- build and test artefacts ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
htmlcov
.coverage

# ---- not needed to run the service ----
tests
conftest.py
archihub/plugins/*/tests
tools
node_modules

# ---- documentation and notes ----
*.md
!README.md

# A plugin's own settings file, for the same reason as the root `.env`: it holds
# credentials, and a deployment injects them as environment variables rather
# than having them baked into an image layer.
archihub/plugins/*/.env
